## Why This Is Asked
Tests multi-source timestamp normalization, Parquet partitioning strategies, and foundational data quality practices—core competencies for entry-level data engineers working with real-world SaaS integrations.

## Key Concepts
- Cross-source timestamp normalization to UTC
- AWS Glue ETL jobs and Data Catalog integration
- Parquet file format with date-based partitioning
- Schema evolution via crawler configuration
- Basic data quality validation and testing frameworks

## Code Example
```javascript
function normalizeTimestamp(ts, formats) {
  // Parse multiple timestamp formats
  for (const format of formats) {
    const parsed = moment(ts, format, true);
    if (parsed.isValid()) {
      return parsed.utc().format();
    }
  }
  throw new Error(`Unable to parse timestamp: ${ts}`);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses ability to design real-time data quality and drift detection at scale, balancing schema evolution, validation, quarantine, alerting, and cross-account governance using AWS services.

## Key Concepts
- Schema evolution and registry management
- Real-time validation and data quarantining
- Observability: CloudWatch metrics and SNS alerts
- Cross-account auditability via Glue Data Catalog and Lake Formation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo validator for a streaming record
function isRecordValid(r){
  if(!r.user_id || !r.timestamp) return false;
  if(typeof r.value !== 'number' || r.value < 0) return false;
  return true;
}
```

